'''Teedo''' was a [[Color|green-skinned]] [[humanoid]] [[scavenger]] who operated in the wastes of the [[desert]] [[Planet|world]] of [[Jakku]] approximately thirty [[Standard year|years]] after [[Battle of Endor]].<ref name="Set to Roll">{{SW|url=news/star-wars-episode-vii-set-to-roll-cameras-may-2014|text=Star Wars: Episode VII Set to Roll Cameras May 2014}}</ref> Like the rest of his [[species]], which was also known as [[Teedo]], Teedo had a strange sense of identity that led him to refer to himself as Teedo.<ref name="Visual" /> Teedo rode a [[luggabeast]] as a beast of burden.

In [[34 ABY]], the [[astromech droid]] [[BB-8]] was caught in a net on Teedo's luggabeast, leading fellow scavenger [[Rey Skywalker|Rey]] to free the [[droid]].<ref name="Name Confirmations" /> The next morning, Teedo and two other bandits attempted to steal BB-8 from Rey as they left [[Hellhound Two|her home]] for [[Niima Outpost]]. Rey escaped Teedo by getting him to follow her into a crashed [[Star Destroyer]], where his [[speeder bike]] was eaten by a [[nightwatcher worm]].<ref name="BB-8 Bandits">{{FOD|BB-8 Bandits}}</ref>

==Behind the scenes==
Teedo is portrayed by [[Kiran Shah]] and voiced by [[David Acord]] in the 2015 film {{Film|VII}}. Shah wore a full-body suit to portray the character.<ref name="Name Confirmations" />

